{"name":"Vin Rouge","hex":"#955264","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rouge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish pink colour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Red or pink makeup to add colour to the cheeks; blusher.","Any reddish pink colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rouge"}],"entries":[{"title":"French wine","blocks":[{"text":"French wine is produced throughout all of France in quantities between 50 and 60 million hectolitres per year, or 7–8 billion bottles. France is one of the largest wine producers in the world. French wine traces its history to the 6th century BCE, with many of France's regions dating their wine-making history to Roman times. The wines produced range from expensive wines sold internationally to modest wines usually only seen within France such as the Margnat wines of the post-war period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/French_taste_of_wines.JPG/330px-French_taste_of_wines.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_wine","wikidata":"Q630531"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg/500px-A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg/1280px-A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgun